  <item>
    <title>William Basinski – Passing the Cup of Sorrows</title>
    <link>https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/william-basinski-passing-the-cup-of-sorrows/</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="true">https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/william-basinski-passing-the-cup-of-sorrows/</guid>
    <pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 05:01:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <enclosure url="https://media.pitchfork.com/photos/6ae4bc8c00019c3ef93fb729/16:9/w_1280,c_limit/William%20Basinski%20-%20Passing%20the%20Cup%20of%20Sorrows.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/>
    <description><![CDATA[<p>The Disintegration Loops made the composer’s name synonymous with weighty meditations on memory and loss, but his latest album—calm, focused, tender—is a reminder of his fondness for beauty.</p>
<img src="https://media.pitchfork.com/photos/6ae4bc8c00019c3ef93fb729/16:9/w_1280,c_limit/William%20Basinski%20-%20Passing%20the%20Cup%20of%20Sorrows.jpg" alt="Passing the Cup of Sorrows cover"/>
